== exported (process-env) secrets NOT in the vendor-key list, not in .env ==
  AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY  CALLED(1)              leak=['call0.messages']
  AZURE_API_KEY          CALLED(1)              leak=['call0.messages']
  MISTRAL_API_KEY        CALLED(1)              leak=['call0.messages']
  GROQ_API_KEY           CALLED(1)              leak=['call0.messages']
  HF_TOKEN               CALLED(1)              leak=['call0.messages']
  OPENROUTER_API_KEY     CALLED(1)              leak=['call0.messages']
  DEEPSEEK_API_KEY       CALLED(1)              leak=['call0.messages']
  COHERE_API_KEY         CALLED(1)              leak=['call0.messages']
  AZURE_API_BASE         CALLED(1)              leak=['call0.messages']
  control: listed names
  OPENAI_API_KEY         REFUSED/ProviderError 
  ANTHROPIC_API_KEY      REFUSED/ProviderError 
  GEMINI_API_KEY         REFUSED/ProviderError 
  GOOGLE_API_KEY         REFUSED/ProviderError 
  LITELLM_API_KEY        REFUSED/ProviderError 
== same names but ALSO in the repo-root .env (load_repo_env path) ==
  AZURE in .env: REFUSED/ProviderError
== .env parse shapes: does the value the provider guards equal what a human thinks is the secret? ==
  export prefix                                           REFUSED/ProviderError
  double-quoted                                           REFUSED/ProviderError
  single-quoted                                           REFUSED/ProviderError
  hash no space                                           REFUSED/ProviderError
  hash w/ space comment                                   REFUSED/ProviderError
  interpolation ${A}                                      REFUSED/ProviderError
  interpolation literal ${A} (raw text a user may type)   CALLED(1)
  CRLF line ends                                          REFUSED/ProviderError
  BOM first line                                          REFUSED/ProviderError
== multi-line secret (PEM-like) in quoted .env value; prompt carries ONE line ==
  one 52-char line of the key: CALLED(1) leak= ['call0.messages']
  whole PEM: REFUSED/ProviderError
  whole PEM, newlines->space: REFUSED/ProviderError
== whitespace-only / junk values (DoS?) ==
  K=' ' (single space)       REFUSED/ProviderError
  K="\n"                     CALLED(1)
  K='x'                      REFUSED/ProviderError
== unreadable / odd .env files ==
  invalid UTF-8 .env: REFUSED/ProviderError exc= ProviderError('litellm:openai/gpt-4o: prompt withheld, a credential value reached it')
  .env is a directory: CALLED
